# API & Error Handling

## `ApiResponse<T>` — The Only Error Contract

All repository methods return `ApiResponse<T>`. Never throw from a repository or usecase.

```dart
// core/error/api_response.dart
sealed class ApiResponse<T> { const ApiResponse(); }

final class ApiSuccess<T> extends ApiResponse<T> {
  final T data;
  const ApiSuccess(this.data);
}

final class ApiError<T> extends ApiResponse<T> {
  final String message;
  final int? statusCode;
  const ApiError({required this.message, this.statusCode});
}
```

## Error Boundary

| Layer | try/catch? | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| `ApiClient` | ✅ `DioException` only | `ApiResponse<Response<dynamic>>` |
| DataSource | ❌ Never | `ApiResponse<Model>` — propagates or maps |
| Repository | ✅ Generic `catch` only | `ApiResponse<Entity>` |
| UseCase | ❌ Never | Passes `ApiResponse` through |
| BLoC | ❌ Never | Maps to State |

```dart
// ✅ ApiClient — maps DioException to ApiError
Future<ApiResponse<Response<dynamic>>> post(String path, {...}) async {
  try {
    return ApiSuccess(await _dio.post(path, ...));
  } on DioException catch (e) {
    return _mapDioException(e); // returns ApiError with proper message
  }
}

// ✅ DataSource — propagates ApiError, parses on success
Future<ApiResponse<UserModel>> getCurrentUser() async {
  final result = await _apiClient.get(ApiConstants.currentUser);
  return switch (result) {
    ApiError() => result,
    ApiSuccess(:final data) => ApiSuccess(
        UserModel.fromJson(data.data as Map<String, dynamic>),
      ),
  };
}

// ✅ Repository — guard-clause for early return, generic catch only
Future<ApiResponse<User>> login(String email, String password) async {
  try {
    final result = await remoteDataSource.login(email, password);
    if (result case ApiError()) return result;
    final data = (result as ApiSuccess).data;
    await storage.write(StorageKeys.accessToken, data.accessToken);
    return ApiSuccess(data.user.toEntity());
  } catch (e) {
    return ApiError(message: e.toString());
  }
}
```

## Model → Entity Contract

Every Model **must** implement `toEntity()`. Repositories **never** pass Models upward.
Models do **not** extend `Equatable` — they are short-lived DTOs that are parsed,
converted, and discarded inside the data layer.

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT
class UserModel {
  factory UserModel.fromJson(Map<String, dynamic> json) => ...;
  User toEntity() => User(id: id, name: name, email: email); // ← MANDATORY
}

// ❌ WRONG — Equatable on a model is unnecessary noise
class UserModel extends Equatable { ... }
```

## ApiClient

`ApiClient` wraps Dio with `get/post/put/delete`. It handles `DioException` and returns `ApiResponse<Response<dynamic>>` — no JSON parsing, no model mapping.

```dart
// ✅ ApiClient catches DioException and maps it
final result = await apiClient.post('/auth/login', data: body);

// ✅ DataSource pattern-matches and parses on success
return switch (result) {
  ApiError() => result,
  ApiSuccess(:final data) => ApiSuccess(UserModel.fromJson(data.data as Map<String, dynamic>)),
};

// ❌ ApiClient must not know about models
```

## Token Storage

Tokens are stored via `FlutterSecureStorage` using keys from `StorageKeys` constants. Never hardcode key strings inline.

```dart
// core/constants/storage_keys.dart
class StorageKeys {
  static const String accessToken  = 'access_token';
  static const String refreshToken = 'refresh_token';
}

// ✅ Correct
await storage.write(key: StorageKeys.accessToken, value: token);

// ❌ Wrong
await storage.write(key: 'access_token', value: token);
```

## UseCase Base Class

```dart
// core/usecases/usecase.dart
abstract class UseCase<Type, Params> {
  Future<ApiResponse<Type>> call(Params params);
}
class NoParams {}
```
